---
description: A set of proposed spikes is not an open spike and not a roadmap
alwaysApply: true
---

# Proposed spikes

`proposed-spikes.yaml` holds one set of proposals and follows `proposed-spikes.template.yaml`. Each item is one proposed spike. The file is not a spike contract, not a result record, and not permission to change the project.

- A proposal has no `status`. It is not `open`, `closed`, or `dropped`.
- Keep result fields off the set: no `created`, `closed`, or `documentation`.
- Each proposal has one `goal.statement`, one `source.question`, and a non-empty `out_of_scope`.
- The user decides which proposal, if any, becomes the next spike. Do not open one on your own.
- Opening copies that proposal into a new `spikes/sN.yaml` and sets `status: open`. The set does not bypass the one-open-spike gate.
- With no open spike, writing `proposed-spikes.yaml` is allowed. Other project files stay unchanged until a spike is open.

```yaml
# ❌ a second contract, or a sequence treated as the plan of record
status: open
documentation:
  decision: |
    Ship these three in order.

# ✅ one proposal inside the set
id: ""
title: ""
goal:
  statement: |
    <one outcome in the project>
  out_of_scope:
    - "<excluded work>"
source:
  question: |
    <exactly one unknown>
```
